  "preamble": "In Faroese, the velar stop /k/ (from Old Norse g) is palatalized to the postalveolar affricate before front vowels and /j/. Because Faroese lenis stops are voiceless and unaspirated, Old Norse [ɡ] before a front vowel now surfaces as [t͡ʃ], which contrasts with aspirated [t͡ʃʰ] from Old Norse k. The earlier Gulf Arabic example (rifig > rifich) has been removed. It could not be verified, and Gulf Arabic *q > g goes on to voiced [d͡ʒ], not [t͡ʃ].",
